**/*.html
**/*.json
!appsscript.json
!index.html
# Node-side dev tests. rootDir is "." here and this list does not exclude JS by extension, so without
# this rule a tests/*.js would be pushed into the Apps Script project as source.
tests/
tests/**
.claude/
.claude/**
clasp.sh

# Node-side DEV SERVER, synced in from gx-theme on 2026-09-03 (commit 333000c). Same failure mode as
# tests/ above: rootDir is "." and nothing here excludes JS by extension, so clasp pushes serve.js as
# serve.gs, where `#!/usr/bin/env node` on line 1 is a parse error that blocks the ENTIRE push —
# backend fix and all. It fired for real in sales the same day.
#
# Armed by the file LANDING, not by any change to this app, so it would have stopped the next deploy
# whatever that deploy carried, and the error would have pointed at a file nobody had touched.
#
# THIS RULE IS NEEDED HERE AND IN SALES, AND NOWHERE ELSE. An earlier version of this comment said
# every spoke that syncs needs its own copy. That was wrong, twice over, and both mistakes were the
# same shape — testing for one spelling of a thing rather than for the mechanism:
#   · spiff, crew and pricecards set rootDir to "apps-script", so a ROOT-level serve.js is never in
#     the push at all. I first reported spiff as armed by assuming rootDir is always ".".
#   · performance uses an ALLOWLIST .claspignore ("**" then !index.html, !goals.gs …), which
#     excludes serve.js without ever naming it. A "does .claspignore mention serve.js" check calls
#     that armed when it is structurally immune.
# Measured against all six repos with serve.js forced present: every one is safe. inventory and
# sales are the only two that needed a named rule, because they are the only two that combine a
# repo-root rootDir with a DENYLIST .claspignore.
#
# The real category is narrower than "JS by extension" and worth stating: clasp pushes .js/.gs/.ts/
# .html/.json and ignores everything else, and serve.js is the first root-level .js file gx-sync has
# ever placed. deploy.sh, gx-preflight.sh and gxengine.sh are .sh; serve.py is .py. Months of clean
# syncs were extension, not vigilance. gx-theme's gx-sync.sh now warns at the moment such a file
# lands (0a53356), which is the durable fix; this rule is the local one.
serve.js
